  <bpmn:process id="Process_40" name="Recommended Price Calculation" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Calculation detail for BPMN-36. Sources: SRS 4.14 FR-PRICE-01–14, FR-PRICE-16 and FR-PRICE-18; app/pricing-state.js P.breakdown and P.cost. Authorized Owner access is a precondition. Read current saved inputs when the owner views product details. Validate positive recipe quantities, available nonnegative recorded costs and utility overhead, and valid configured markup. Count each applicable packaging item once. Missing required data yields Unavailable. Exclude delivery, marketing and other nonproduction costs. Preserve precision through calculation; calculate the recommendation as 5 × ceiling(raw price ÷ 5). Exact multiples of ₱5 stay the same. This proposed Kitchen406 rule uses a smaller upward adjustment than ₱10 increments; the prototype rounds to two decimals. Local price-point example: the Mary Grace menu lists Butter Chiffon at ₱75 per piece and Banana Bread at ₱85 per slice (https://dkghjxf1hor4.cloudfront.net/web/production/pdfs/sitecontent/5/mg-website-menu-122025_rev.pdf). These examples illustrate price points, not the bakery’s rounding policy. Margin shown here uses the rounded recommendation and is unavailable if that value is zero. The owner can apply the recommendation or enter a different price. Use the positive-price validation and current-record checks from BPMN-36 before saving the selected final price separately from the recommendation. On validation or save failure, retain the current saved price and allow the owner to retry the price selection or finish by viewing the current product price. The recommendation is calculated once per flow.</bpmn:documentation>
